meta {
  name: 01-auth-journey
  seq: 2
}

docs {
  The account lifecycle over real HTTP, as a client experiences it.

  This folder registers its OWN throwaway user each run (a timestamped address),
  rather than using a seeded one. That is deliberate: registration and the
  unverified-login rejection can only be observed on an account whose history
  the run controls. The seeded accounts are already verified and so can never
  exercise this path.

  The one thing it cannot do is verify that address — tokens go only to the
  console email backend. Everything after verification is therefore tested with
  the pre-verified seeded principals instead.
}
